// Tradeable goods.
//
// Quantities and prices are whole numbers — you can't own half a loaf. Prices
// are in coins; base values are scaled so price has integer resolution as stock
// moves.
//
//   name         display / lookup id
//   base_price   coins per unit when stock sits at `target_stock`
//   target_stock stock level the price is anchored to (scarcer -> dearer)
//   nutrition    sustenance restored per unit eaten (0 = inedible; a need meter,
//                so this one is continuous)
[
    // Grain is a raw material — you farm it, but you don't eat it raw. It must be
    // baked into bread, so a farm -> bake -> eat production chain (and a division
    // of labour between growing and baking) emerges from people's food goals.
    (name: "grain", base_price: 10, target_stock: 40, nutrition: 0.0),
    (name: "bread", base_price: 30, target_stock: 25, nutrition: 45.0),
]
